# CLAUDE.md hygiene

`CLAUDE.md` Session State is short. Detailed findings live in `sessions_summary/`. The full policy: `sessions_summary/POLICY.md`.

## Hard rule

Do not write findings directly into `CLAUDE.md` Session State. Write them to the archive first, then update Session State to point at it. Session State holds pointers; archive holds data.

## Status taxonomy

Every work block is one of `active` / `paused` / `closed` / `superseded`. Status lives in `CLAUDE.md` Session State and in the archive front-matter.

## Three-layer knowledge hierarchy

See `sessions_summary/POLICY.md` §Operator role and §Three-layer knowledge hierarchy.

| Layer | Storage | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| Permanent structural knowledge | `wiki/` | Principles, architecture, domain facts |
| Decision rationale | `docs/decisions.md`, `docs/adr/` | Why things were built this way |
| Session digest | `sessions_summary/YYYY-MM-DD-digest.md` | One-session findings, cross-session continuity |
